# Mobile-first surface (repo-wide)

<!--
  Callers: every Cursor agent session (alwaysApply).
  SoT: docs/mobile-first/SURFACE_LAW.md
  User: "span repo-wide" / "do everything on the mobile app first."
-->

**SoT:** [`docs/mobile-first/SURFACE_LAW.md`](../../docs/mobile-first/SURFACE_LAW.md)  
**Checklist:** `src/lib/mobile/mobile-first-surface.ts`

## Binding rule

Every operator verb in this product must be completable on the **mobile web
app (`/m/*`) first**. Desktop desks, stations, and kiosk faces consume that
SoT (phone-width frame + gutters / compact recents) — they do not invent a
second IA phones cannot run. Warehouse OS is one domain among many; this law
is **repo-wide**.

## When building or reviewing UI

1. Classify the job: **A** floor `/m`, **B** phone browse, **C** dense desk,
   **D** station/kiosk (`SURFACE_LAW` §3).
2. New or ported verbs: ship **A/B under `/m`** before treating C/D as done.
3. Desktop large viewports: **phone frame pattern** — fixed phone column,
   thick side gutters; compact recents top-left only — not a full desk rail.
4. **One job / sticky CTA / token family per use case** (TabSwitch ≠ path chips
   ≠ TableTabs). See `SURFACE_LAW` §5–§6.
5. No hover-only; no dual `lg:hidden` + `hidden lg:block` full flows.
6. `ds_contract` / `ds_tokens` / `ds_critique` before `src/**/*.{tsx,jsx,css}` writes.
7. Prefer existing `/m` kit: `RedesignedMobileShell`, Pick (`/m/pick`), Work
   (`/m/work`), item-record mobile, `BottomSheet`, `IconButton size="touch"`.

## Refuse

- “Desktop-only; mobile later.”
- Desktop-shrunk desks called mobile-first.
- Parallel mobile design systems outside `src/components/mobile/` + DS pins.

## Start URLs

- Pick queue: `/m/pick`
- Pick session: `/m/pick/[orderId]`
- Orders: `/m/work`
